    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// One adapter region, expanded by the package the header names." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `syntax doubled { c4 }` is not ordinary Musa: the region's contents are read" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// by the fixed lexer and grouper and handed to `std::adapters::doubled`, which" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// answers with `(repeated(c4, 2), 0)` — the contents twice, and the anchor of the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// group they were rebuilt from. Everything after that is ordinary — the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// expression is resolved, checked, and evaluated exactly as if it had been" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// written here, which is what makes an adapter a reader rather than a second" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// language." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The anchor is a number, and the number is only a place when the compiler's" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// own table says so. That is how a value an expansion produced remembers where" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// it came from without the adapter ever being able to read a range." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Doubled\"" },
    { "kind": "{", "text": "{" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The adapter names `repeated` in what it writes, and an adapter's output is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// resolved here, in this file's scope: what it calls, this file imports." },
